OL,3,GNEWSAHow one grandmother stays positive
OL,4,Adespite three bouts of cancer
OL,5,
OL,6,FWhen Kirsty Priest was told she had
OL,7,Fcancer for a third time in 15 years,
OL,8,Fshe thought: "What have I done to
OL,9,Fdeserve this? I must be a really bad
OL,10,Fperson."
OL,12,FShe was treated twice for separate
OL,13,Fcases of breast cancer, 10 years apart,
OL,14,Fbut earlier this year was told she had
OL,15,Fa brain tumour.
OL,17,FOn top of that, she found out during
OL,18,Fher earlier treatment that she had a
OL,19,Fmutated gene which could double her
OL,20,Frisk of further breast cancer, meaning
OL,21,Fregular treatments for the rest of her
OL,22,Flife.
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
